# e2e/.env.golden-roundtrip.example — the golden-path PR round-trip demo gate
# env (#1239).
#
# The three specs below encode the exact demo we sell: a signed `pull_request`
# webhook → build dispatched ≤15s → SSE log delta in the UI → `success` commit
# status on the PR HEAD SHA (never the base SHA) → target_url resolving to
# /builds/:id. They are CORRECT but `test.skip()` until the provisioning vars
# below are set, so they never run green by themselves.
#
#   - specs/v3/55-golden-path-pr-roundtrip.spec.ts › `happy` (seam guard)
#   - specs/v3/40-github-app-golden-path.spec.ts    › SUCCESS + ci/titan legs
#   - specs/v3/50-github-pr-roundtrip.spec.ts       › real `gh pr create`
#
# DO NOT put real secrets here — this file is committed. Copy it to a
# gitignored `e2e/.env.golden-roundtrip`, fill it, and run:
#
#   task rig:smoke:golden-roundtrip
#
# (the task sources e2e/.env.golden-roundtrip automatically). Or export the
# vars by hand and run the same task.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Opt-in + rig target
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The opt-in switch. The gate refuses to run (exit 0, graceful skip) unless this
# is set, so a plain local dev box never posts webhooks / polls real GitHub.
LAYER2_RIG_AVAILABLE=1

# Which rig the round-trip is driven against. Defaults are handled by the e2e
# fixtures (local docker rig at http://localhost:5180). Point at the public k3s
# rig for the real demo gate:
# TITAN_RIG_URL=https://titan.test.example.com

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provisioning vars (REQUIRED — from registering + installing the GitHub App)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The gate FAILS CLOSED (exit 3, naming the missing var) if any of these is
# unset while opted in — a missing var must never degrade silently to a green
# skip. Retrieve them once the App is registered + installed on the rig:
#
#   TITAN_E2E_GH_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET — the App's webhook secret (used to sign the
#     synthetic pull_request payload spec 55 POSTs). Read it from the rig's App
#     config / the secret you set at registration time. NOT read from the rig DB
#     by the spec — you must supply it.
#
#   TITAN_E2E_GH_INSTALLATION_ID — the numeric installation id of the App on the
#     fixture repo. From the rig: GET /api/v1/github-app/installations, or the
#     install URL .../installations/<ID>.
#
#   TITAN_E2E_GH_REPO_ID — the numeric GitHub repo id of the fixture repo so the
#     synthetic payload references a real linked repo. From:
#       gh api /repos/hadamrd/titan-e2e-fixture --jq .id
#
TITAN_E2E_GH_APP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=<app-webhook-secret>
TITAN_E2E_GH_INSTALLATION_ID=<installation-id>
TITAN_E2E_GH_REPO_ID=<repo-id>

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The fixture repo the specs poll for commit statuses. Default below.
# TITAN_E2E_FIXTURE_REPO=hadamrd/titan-e2e-fixture

# Per-test timeout (ms). The gate defaults to 1_200_000 (20 min) like
# rig:smoke:real — real GitHub App webhook + k3s scheduling is slow.
# TITAN_TEST_TIMEOUT_MS=1200000
